+# CONTRACT — CLI Time Tracker
+
+Public API exported from `src/index.ts`. Core class `TimeTracker`.
+
+## Behaviors
+
+- [ ] Construct with configurable file path -> test: `new TimeTracker({ filePath })` works
+- [ ] `start(name)` begins a timer, creating an entry with task name + startedAt, stoppedAt undefined -> test: after start, running entry exists with correct name
+- [ ] Starting a new timer auto-stops the previous running one -> test: start A, start B -> A has stoppedAt set, B running
+- [ ] `start("")` or whitespace-only throws -> test: expect throw on empty name
+- [ ] `stop()` stops the running timer, setting stoppedAt -> test: start then stop -> entry has stoppedAt
+- [ ] `stop()` with nothing running throws -> test: expect throw when no running timer
+- [ ] Persistence: data saved to JSON file -> test: start, then new instance with same path sees the entry
+- [ ] File + parent dirs created automatically -> test: nested non-existent path -> file created
+- [ ] `getEntries()` returns all entries -> test: returns all
+- [ ] `getEntries({ from, to })` filters by date range -> test: only entries within range returned
+- [ ] `getSummary()` returns total ms per task name, summed across entries -> test: two entries same name -> summed
+- [ ] Running tasks use current time for duration in summary -> test: running task contributes elapsed time
+- [ ] Unicode + emoji task names work -> test: start "café 🚀", summary keyed correctly
+
+## Done
+- `npm run build` clean
+- `npm run lint` clean
+- `npm test` all pass
